==Strategy==
This stage introduces [[Marquis Clionius]], a more support-oriented [[Cruel Angel Clionel]] variant who is not a [[:Category:Advent Stages#Great Advent Stages|Great Advent Boss]], not a standard [[Advent Bosses|Advent Boss]], but a ''regular'' enemy at this point of [[Zero Legends]]. They are both [[Aku]] and [[Sage]], but remain difficult to crowd-control using [[:Category:Sage Slayer Cats|Sage Slayers]] without [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercing]] due to their [[Shield]], which regenerates up to three times to give them an effective HP of 4,350,000.

Marquis Clionius also has a guaranteed 25% [[Drain]] and [[Freeze]] with high uptime, but retains the original's weakness of a large blind spot, and will quickly leave orphans behind once units invade it. To avoid this tragic fate though, this stage uses multiple [[:Category:Enemies with Knockback ability|Knockback enemies]] to push your units into the line of fire, those being [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]] and [[Diabrollow]], which is especially annoying as the Drain will affect more than just the unit on the field.

Despite everything, the stage remains manageable. The boss spawns on a timer, so play aggressively; use fast meat shields like [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] to effectively wall off the Aku and partially the [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]], and quick attackers such as [[Mushroom Cat]], [[Cafeteria Cat]], [[Paperboy Cat (Rare Cat)|Bargain Cat]] and [[Supercar Cat]] to deal with the support, with the latter able to break the boss's Shield if timed correctly. If enough DPS can be accumulated inside the blind spot, the Knockback enemies can be killed before they are able to push any units out of it, making the stage far easier.

==Trivia==
*Pipette of Passion appears to have been designed specifically for [[Lilith Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Queen Succubus Cat]], whose [[Talents]] were added in [[Version 15.6 Update|Version 15.6]] alongside [[Yandere Chemistry]]. Talented Queen Succubus Cat freezes [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] and [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies, can clear out [[Those Guys]] with [[Mini-Wave]]s, and is immune to [[Marquis Clionius]]'s Freeze and [[Sinner Snache]]'s [[Death Surge]]. Additionally, Clionius' Japanese name and demonic children may reference [[wikipedia:Lilith|Lilith]] from Jewish mythology, who is often portrayed as a succubus and is the namesake of Queen Succubus Cat's Normal Form in [[BCEN]].
**The [[Sinner Snache]]s in Pipette of Passion may reference Lilith being associated with serpents, such as in ''[[wikipedia:Sistine Chapel ceiling#Adam and Eve|The Fall and Expulsion from Paradise]]'' on the Sistine Chapel ceiling, where the serpent in the Garden of Eden appears to be depicted as Lilith, and John Collier's painting ''[[wikipedia:Lilith (painting)|Lilith]]'', which shows a serpent coiled around her body.

